@page "/"

<PageTitle>Wick</PageTitle>

<h1>Wick</h1>
<p class="lead">
    State classes marked <code>[ReactiveState]</code> with <code>partial</code> properties track who reads them.
    Components inheriting <code>ReactiveComponentBase</code> (every component here, through <code>_Imports.razor</code>)
    re-render when something they read during their last render changes, from any thread, with no events,
    subscriptions or <code>StateHasChanged</code> calls.
</p>

<pre class="card"><code>[ReactiveState]
public sealed partial class CounterState
{
    public partial int Count { get; set; }
}</code></pre>

<p>
    Badges like <RenderCount Value="++_renders" /> count how many times a component rendered and flash when it renders.
</p>

<div class="cards">
    <div class="card">
        <h2><NavLink href="counter">Counter</NavLink></h2>
        <p>Sync and async handlers, thread-pool writes, 100,000 concurrent writes, computed properties.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2><NavLink href="grid">Fine-grained grid</NavLink></h2>
        <p>400 cells: one render per change, next to the classic event pattern that re-renders all of them.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2><NavLink href="market">Live market</NavLink></h2>
        <p>A singleton written by a background service, shared by every tab, with batched ticks.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2><NavLink href="profile">Nested state</NavLink></h2>
        <p>Reactive objects inside reactive objects, two-way binding, and dependencies that come and go.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2><NavLink href="todos">Todo list</NavLink></h2>
        <p>A reactive list, cached derived values, an effect, and batched bulk updates.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2><NavLink href="search">Async effects</NavLink></h2>
        <p>Search as you type with cancellation and ordered runs, and JavaScript interop from an effect.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2><NavLink href="timing">Listener timing</NavLink></h2>
        <p>A debounced autosave that flushes on demand and on dispose, a throttled preview, and a debounced value.</p>
